      "writtenOn": "2025-08-08T21:14:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I have concerns about this and how it relates to multiple tests in parallel. This currently isn\u0027t an issue since all the tests are technically a single test (`TestFSTestOSWrapper_MkdirTemp`) as far as `go test` is concerned, and so you don\u0027t have any risk of race conditions. However, if/when another test is added that calls this or `MkdirTemp` and relies on a specific directory name, we could run into flaky test failures. E.g. if both tests are expecting `/tmp/test-1` as the directory name and the following happens:\n\n```\nResetTempCounterForTesting() // test 1\nResetTempCounterForTesting() // test 2\nMkdirTemp() // test 1\nMkdirTemp() // test 2\n```\n\ntest 2 would fail since it would get `/tmp/test-2`. I think there are two ways you could go about this:\n\n1. Relax the checks to allow for any numerical component instead of a specific number, e.g. the regex `temp-\\d+`. I think this would be the preferred option.\n2. If you really need to check for a specific value, add a global mutex that all tests which rely on `MkdirTemp` must acquire at the start of the test.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 371,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 371,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "848f0ab109da7b93960af721286450e4bc7453dc",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c9c73493_4ad03e1e",
        "filename": "tools/src/oswrapper/fstestoswrapper.go",
