      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-13T17:48:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I agree this is a concern and #1 is the better option. Introducing a global mutex for this feels overkill/error prone.\n\nI have rewritten the test runner to only check that the random part is a u32.\n\nI have removed ResetTempCounterForTesting() entirely, since it is no longer used in the tests, and gives the false impression of thread/concurrency safety.",
